chore(kit): say why the catalogue cache stored nothing

The two slots are written and read through one path, and until now that path
said nothing at all: `write` dropped an encode failure through `try?` without a
trace, `record` collapsed absent, undecodable, foreign and stale into one `nil`,
and both `persist*` guards returned in silence. So "the app catalogue does not
survive a relaunch" and "the store was never asked to write anything" look
identical from the outside — which is exactly the question that could not be
answered by reading the code.

Each of those now names itself once. `warmCatalogues` reports what came off
disk, including the case where the session has no store at all, because that one
disables both slots at once and reads as a cache that simply does not work.
`storeRefusal` lists every reason a store call refused rather than the first: an
empty list and a missing identity are very different bugs and a `guard` that
stops at the first would hide the second.

Diagnostics only — no behaviour changes.

